const INT = {"Epinephrine":"Beta blockers blunt response; MAOIs and tricyclics increase hypertensive effect.","Glucagon":"Warfarin effect may increase; less effective with depleted glycogen (alcohol, starvation).","Carbidopa-levodopa":"MAOIs (hypertensive crisis); antipsychotics and metoclopramide oppose it; protein and pyridoxine reduce absorption.","Pyridostigmine":"Anticholinergics oppose it; some antibiotics (aminoglycosides) worsen weakness.","Donepezil":"Anticholinergics oppose it; NSAIDs add GI bleeding risk; beta blockers add bradycardia.","Levetiracetam":"Alcohol and other CNS depressants add sedation.","Valproic acid":"Raises lamotrigine and phenobarbital levels; aspirin raises free valproate; carbapenems lower levels.","Carbamazepine":"Induces liver enzymes — lowers levels of oral contraceptives, warfarin, many drugs; grapefruit raises its level.","Rifampin":"Induces liver enzymes — lowers oral contraceptives, warfarin, methadone, many antiretrovirals.","Ethambutol":"Aluminum antacids reduce absorption.","Methimazole / propylthiouracil":"Changes warfarin and digoxin needs as thyroid levels normalize.","Hydrocortisone":"NSAIDs (GI bleeding); loop diuretics (hypokalemia); raises glucose — insulin needs rise.","Desmopressin":"Carbamazepine, SSRIs, NSAIDs increase hyponatremia risk.","Risperidone":"CNS depressants add sedation; QT-prolonging drugs; levodopa opposes it.","Benztropine":"Other anticholinergics (antihistamines, tricyclics) add effects.","Disulfiram":"Any alcohol; metronidazole; raises phenytoin and warfarin levels.","Buprenorphine":"Benzodiazepines, alcohol, other depressants (respiratory depression); can precipitate withdrawal if full agonists are on board.","Ferrous sulfate":"Antacids, PPIs, calcium, dairy, tea reduce absorption; separate from tetracyclines, fluoroquinolones, levothyroxine.","Cyanocobalamin":"Metformin, PPIs, and colchicine lower B12 absorption.","Filgrastim":"Don't give within 24 hours before or after chemotherapy.","Tamsulosin":"Other antihypertensives and PDE-5 inhibitors (sildenafil) add hypotension.","Nitrofurantoin":"Magnesium antacids reduce absorption.","Phenazopyridine":"Interferes with urine dipstick color tests.","Colchicine":"Clarithromycin, grapefruit, and some azoles raise levels (toxicity).","Methotrexate":"NSAIDs, PPIs, penicillins, TMP-SMX raise levels; alcohol (liver).","Terbutaline":"Beta blockers oppose it; other sympathomimetics add cardiac effects.","Carboprost":"Increases effect of other oxytocic drugs.","Acyclovir":"Other nephrotoxic drugs add kidney risk.","Nystatin":"Few significant interactions."};
